---
description: Prevent local Playwright browser crashes and repeated macOS crash dialogs
alwaysApply: true
---

# Run Playwright outside the sandbox

- On this macOS workspace, run Playwright browser tests outside the sandbox from the first attempt (for example, use the shell tool with `required_permissions: ["all"]`).
- Do not first try `npm run test:e2e`, `CI=1 npm run test:e2e`, or other Playwright browser commands in the sandbox.
- Sandboxed Playwright launches can report a missing Chromium executable and repeatedly abort Firefox or WebKit during retries, producing many "quit unexpectedly" macOS dialogs.
- If a browser launch fails, inspect the first failure before retrying. Do not allow repeated cross-browser retries when the failure is environmental.
